# Dual git remotes (GitHub + gitcore)

This repo is mirrored on **two private remotes**. When the user asks to commit and/or push:

1. Create **one** local commit (do not skip hooks; do not commit `.env` or secrets).
2. Push that commit to **both** remotes. Never GitHub-only or gitcore-only unless the user explicitly says so.
3. Do not force-push. Do not make either remote public.

## Remotes

| Name | Host | URL | Visibility |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `github` | github.com | https://github.com/Gowdabt/rag-platform | **private** |
| `soma` | git.soma.salesforce.com | https://git.soma.salesforce.com/hbt/rag-platform | **private** |
| `all` | both push URLs | `git push all <branch>` | **private** |

GitHub CLI (`gh`) is for **github.com / Gowdabt** only. Salesforce uses git-soma / `GH_HOST=git.soma.salesforce.com` for `hbt/rag-platform`. Do not use github.com `gh` against Salesforce. gitcore.soma.salesforce.com forbids user-account repos (do not publish this personal project into Core orgs).

## Commands

```bash
git push github main
git push soma main
git push all main
```

Use the existing default branch (`main`). Keep both remotes private (`gh repo edit --visibility private` on GitHub if it ever becomes public).
